Dividend Loaning

	Philosophy

		-
			Dividend loaning is the practice of loaning funds or assets to a recipient, where the
			donor reserves the right to reclaim them at will, but for the duration of the loan,
			any income generated from said funds and assets is retained by said recipient.
		-

	Principles

		Incentives

			Growth

				-
					Donors may be incentivized to make dividend loans on the premise that the
					recipient will manage the investment and consequential growth of the loaned
					assets effectively.
				-

			Taxation

				-
					Depending on the nature of the recipients, dividend loans may bestow benefits
					on donors regarding taxation.
				-

		Implementation

			Publicly Tradable Security

				-
					Dividend loaning may take the form of publicly tradable securities.
					
					Such securities may be referred to as altruistic assets.
				-

			Account Management

				-
					Dividend loaning may take the form of utilities, and platforms to administer
					said utilities, which interface with user accounts to automatically disperse
					dividends from selected assets to selected recipients.

					Such utilities and platforms may be referred to as altruistic managers.
				-